  "reason": "qc_gen.py RTL registers every data pin in the S / N strip (bc / rs_i entry flops, bco / rs / rs_o exit flops, rst_n pin register); cid / far are static straps from the instance's own tie cells; landing halves land rsi in 2 stages; every data pin lands in a hard station / half register (flop-first / flop-last)"
 },
 "structural_change": "SQC-CB8 10-22 qfd_c_b8_rgn (PENDING-COORD, die contract not ruled): CB8 = 8 live A0 (a0_rc14face 820.8 x 907.2) as 2 cols x 4 rows (MY | R0 pair sharing corridor A) -> outline 2419.2 x 5227.2 in the die slot 2445.12 x 5227.2; T trunk (rs_i -> rs_o far-band feedthrough + station spine) = a horizontal band (b8n); 8 regional clock roots ck_c<c>r<r> / resets rst_c<c>r<r>; ring tiles + free stations by ring_tile_place_b.py; buses over their pin-register stations at 4 pins/um; clock = cb16_ckring3 regional rings (K 4, BUFx12f_ASAP7_75t_R every 100 um, as rgk); every region crossing a hard landing-ring tile.  Prior: QW-CB16REG 10-20 main line (a): qfd_c_b8n parent with every region crossing HARDENED -- 32 qfd_c_ring516/514 tiles (writer ring on the source region clock + reader incl. output register on the destination clock, one tile per crossing, 2 masters hardened once) replace the 64 soft ring halves of qfd_c_b8n_fulln; each region root now reaches only hard-child clock pins (A0, stations, xstn, ring tiles)",
